# 1. Project Mission

I have an existing Android application developed using Kotlin.

Your mission is to deeply research, audit, evaluate, and prepare this existing Android project for professional publication across all relevant Android application stores and distribution platforms that are compatible with Google AdMob.

The objective is not simply to make the application publishable on Google Play Store.

I want a professionally engineered, secure, policy-compliant, scalable, maintainable, and future-proof Android publishing system that supports one shared application codebase and multiple distribution channels.

The project must be evaluated from five major perspectives:

1. Android application architecture and technical quality.
2. Google AdMob integration and monetization compliance.
3. Multi-store compatibility and publishing requirements.
4. Security, privacy, and legal compliance.
5. Automated build, testing, and release management.

**Critical execution rule: Research and audit first. Implementation must not begin until I explicitly approve the proposed implementation plan.**

