# 18. Definition of Done

The project is considered prepared for publication only when the relevant requirements have been verified.

### Technical Readiness

- Existing application builds successfully.
- Required SDK versions are compatible.
- Gradle configuration is validated.
- Manifest configuration is valid.
- Dependencies are reviewed.
- Release artifacts are generated and verified.

### AdMob Readiness

- SDK configuration is correct.
- App identity is consistent.
- Ad units are configured correctly.
- Consent requirements are addressed.
- Advertising placements follow applicable policies.
- Test and production configurations are separated.
- Store and device compatibility are independently assessed.

### Store Readiness

- Submission requirements are documented.
- Signing requirements are understood.
- Required metadata is prepared.
- Privacy declarations are reviewed.
- Content and intellectual property risks are addressed.
- Platform-specific restrictions are documented.

### Security Readiness

- No exposed signing credentials.
- No unnecessary permissions.
- No unresolved critical security findings.
- Sensitive data handling is reviewed.
- Release configuration is validated.

### Automation Readiness

- Build validation is automated where appropriate.
- Tests run successfully.
- Release artifacts are reproducible or their limitations are documented.
- Signing secrets are protected.
- Publishing requires an explicit approval gate.

A successful local build alone does not mean that an application is approved by an app store or authorized to serve AdMob advertisements.

Keep these statuses separate.

